      <metadata>
        <description><![CDATA[{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs34 AutoColor\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Colours tracks, items, regions and markers, and sets track icons, from their {\b names}: plain substring, glob or {\b regular expression}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Each object type configured by separate set of rules. Within a set the first matching rule wins.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The configuration window requires ReaImGui 0.10+.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Config file stored in {\f1 \fs24 MXM_AutoColor/config.json} under the REAPER resource path, outside Scripts/, to prevent overwriting on update.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \fs24 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIT licensed. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/michal-bartak/Reaper-AutoColor"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
https://github.com/michal-bartak/Reaper-AutoColor
}}}
\par}
}
]]></description>
        <link rel="website" href="https://github.com/michal-bartak/Reaper-AutoColor">GitHub</link>
      </metadata>
